nodecode-agent-router is a rewrite of Pinutss's Pinutss/jev-agent-router:

  https://github.com/Pinutss/jev-agent-router
  commit 8cb6d67a81d4545502750c4599b427d98acf3120
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Pinuts (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole of the original's local router — router.py's
HeuristicRouter and its tokenizer, the stopword list, the access policies
(scope, disabled, already failed, missing capabilities, missing permissions,
forbidden permissions, duplicate input), the weighted score (relevance 0.45,
capabilities 0.25, reliability 0.15, cost 0.10, latency 0.05), the three
decisions with their abstention reasons, the single-hop fallback through a
failed agent's fallback_id, and the MCP tool agent_route with its arguments
and its JSON answer (models.py's AgentProfile, RouteRequest and RouteResult).
The demo registry is kept, in English, so a fresh home has something to rank.

Also rewritten: what the plugin exposed around the tool. The tool schema
became one declared contract, the skill and the command became the same
manual under (help :agent-router) and one slash command, /agents, and the
verbs route, route-json and agents-text are the same decision from eval.

Left out, and why: the remote judges (JEV, the OpenAI-compatible gateways
and the model catalog behind them), the HTTP server at /v1/route and its
demo page, the CLI, the Docker image, the benchmark runner and the regex
secret redaction. All of them exist to rank through a model over the network;
a cell that ranks locally in the same process needs none of them, and no key,
no endpoint and no HTTP client is carried here. Also left out: the
box/shape dispatch by provider (local, mock, custom, jev) — this cell ships
the one provider the shipped plugin itself defaults to, local.
